## Web interface

`interfaces/web.py` is a thin FastAPI app (`{{ project_slug }} serve`):

- `GET /chat?message=...&stream=true` — Server-Sent Events. With `stream=true`
  (default) the assistant's answer is streamed **token-by-token** (`event: token`)
  for a live typing effect; tool calls/results and a `final` event (answer +
  token/cost stats) are always emitted. The loop runs in a worker thread and
  pushes events onto a queue. Token streaming rides on `loop.run(on_delta=...)`,
  which calls the client's `stream()` instead of `complete()`. Set `stream=false`
  for a single non-streamed response.
- `GET|POST /config` — read/edit the **runtime behavioral** config (the same
  fields as `config.yaml`). Edits apply in-process; restart reloads from disk.
  Secrets are never returned or editable — profiles only carry env-var names.

The CLI streams too: `{{ project_slug }} run --stream "..."`. To stream from your
own code, pass `on_delta` (a `Callable[[str], None]`) to `run()`.

To add a structural change (a new endpoint, a new module), edit `web.py`
directly — it's yours. Behavioral knobs belong in `config.yaml` / the panel.{% endif %}{% if spec.mcp.enabled %}
## MCP tools

`harness/mcp.py` connects [MCP](https://modelcontextprotocol.io) servers and
registers their tools into the same registry as built-in tools — the loop is
untouched. Add servers in `config.yaml` (a runtime knob; no regeneration):

```yaml
mcp:
  servers:
    - name: filesystem            # stdio: launched as a subprocess
      command: npx
      args: ["-y", "@modelcontextprotocol/server-filesystem", "/data"]
    - name: github                # remote Streamable HTTP
      url: https://api.example.com/mcp/
      auth_env: GITHUB_MCP_TOKEN  # env-var NAME; the value lives in .env
tools:
  - name: filesystem__list_directory   # allowlist as <server>__<tool>
    enabled: true
```

Transport is chosen per server: `command` -> stdio, `url` -> remote. A discovered
tool is offered to the model **only** when allowlisted in `tools:` as
`<server>__<tool>`; MCP tools default to `risk="high"`, so opt in deliberately.
Secrets (`env` / `auth_env`) are referenced by env-var **name** and resolved from
`.env` at runtime — never stored in `config.yaml`. The `mcp` dependency exists
only because this repo was generated with MCP enabled.{% endif %}
